From 7b570a032de317772c0cf518d305fe27aed3c611 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neivin Detlefsen <neivin.detlefsen@gmx.de>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:34:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] fix: keep a jmp (abs,x) dispatch local while its path
 holds a php

A JMP (abs) / JMP (abs,X) tail dispatch sent each target into a
separate function with an empty PHP history. A target that pops the
dispatcher's PHP then kept the dispatch-site width after its PLP.
FF6's ValidateSpellList (C2:568D) enters with X=1, does PHX; PHP; LONGI
and loops over `JMP (AddToSpellListTbl,X)`; every target ends in the
shared `PLP; PLX; RTS`. The split-off targets pulled X with 16 bits
after a PLP that had restored X=1, S came out one byte off and the RTS
jumped into the zero page.

A plain jump onto a sibling entry is already decoded through while the
path holds a PHP. Do the same for a short dispatch whose targets are
ROM labels in the same bank: mark it as a local computed goto, give the
targets the PHP history of the site, and switch on the pointer read
from PB:(abs + X). Local gotos also accept HiROM targets below $8000.
The Python decoder and the native analyzer apply the same rule.

Regression: tests/v2/test_held_php_dispatch_local.py and the decoder
test dispatch_under_php_keeps_targets_local.
